      "summary": "Product Image Management",
      "description": "As a\n Merchandiser,\nI want\n product images to be stored and managed centrally within SFCC,\nso that\n the storefront can reliably display optimised product imagery across all pages and breakpoints.\nProduct images are uploaded and managed in SFCC BM at the master or variation group (colour) level. Images are served at appropriate resolutions per device breakpoint from a single uploaded source asset. \nVideo content is out of scope — see \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-188\n and \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-302\n . \n\n\n\n\nProduct Image Type\nDescription\nDisplay order (PDP leading)\nHero / Model\nModel view — primary image. Primary on PDP, hover image on PLP\n1\nGhost / Flat\nItem/flat lay view — backgroundless, dynamic background colour. Primary on PLP, secondary on PDP\n2\nDetail\nClose up shot\n3\nProduct Styling Image\n4\n…\n5\n…\n6\nAutomatic swatches for clothing through tagging in Magento today, the tag is “Colour Swatch Images”.\nManual swatches for accessories - content team has to upload swatch images for these.\nRunway / Campaign imagery are also there - they come at the end of the carousel.\nShould be adjustable display order",
